    note: `A static site of up to 100 pages starts from ${P.site} and is enough for a trader with a few hundred products, a shipping information page and an RFQ basket. A large catalogue site with thousands of codes, brand pages and destination content starts from ${P.seoSite}. Buyer logins, tiered price lists visible per account, order history or a live stock view are software rather than website features and start from ${P.software}. A real checkout that takes card payments is an online store from ${P.shop}, and most SAIF Zone companies should not buy one — the model is a quote and a proforma invoice, not a basket and a card. The cut-off logic, the Incoterm fields on the enquiry form, the weight and dimension fields and the performance budget are configuration and sit inside the price rather than on top of it. What moves the number is how many product codes need individual pages, whether pricing is gated, whether your stock data can be exported at all, and whether we write the product copy or you supply it. Everything is quoted as itemised USD lines, nothing is billed before you approve the quote in writing, and the general ladder is on <a href='/uae/website-development-cost/'>website development cost</a>.`,
